      "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/a1250d2f413016c4b4524d50823ef816af9aff40",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "51f5fa7bd539ae3b328b50bf4cd2a3eeb003a3e3",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/trees/51f5fa7bd539ae3b328b50bf4cd2a3eeb003a3e3"
      },
      "verification": {
        "verified": true,
        "reason": "valid",
        "payload": "tree 51f5fa7bd539ae3b328b50bf4cd2a3eeb003a3e3\nparent 5de0c29e06f41f6901fd0d0ec69c9359612371e5\nauthor PraneethGunas <praneethgunas404@gmail.com> 1787591990 -0700\ncommitter PraneethGunas <praneethgunas404@gmail.com> 1787592087 -0700\n\nwallet: Add deriveHDKey interface\n\nExpose deriveHDKey through interfaces::Wallet and add unit coverage for the\ninterface path:\n- deriving at a hardened path returns the xpub and its key origin\n- a path without a hardened step is rejected\n- a path deeper than BIP32 allows is rejected\n- an xpub the wallet does not hold is rejected\n- a wallet with private keys disabled is rejected\n- a locked wallet returns WalletErrorCode::UnlockNeeded\n\nThe interface returns only the xpub. Under the process separation work every\ninterfaces::Wallet call becomes a message on a socket, so an xprv return\nvalue would be serialised into another process and any transport buffer\nalong the way. The derivehdkey RPC keeps calling SelectHDKey() and\nDeriveExtKey() directly, because it reports path failures as\nRPC_INVALID_PARAMETER and needs the extended private key for its `private`\noption.\n",
        "signature": "-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\niJEEABYKADkWIQRfqDW/pLSFogdaX281yQTY7xFXMAUCaox9lxsUgAAAAAAEAA5t\nYW51MiwyLjUrMS4xMiwwLDMACgkQNckE2O8RVzD0FwD/b3xg8VQT3hENwIGmwtrk\nkDWB2H128aaBhqhgybmThpYA/3kZt4LgDtthK8DtXHmPvldbywFhsSpv5bQhn0Om\nj0MK\n=fHe3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----"
      },
      "parents": [
